1
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:03,300
It's just that for you,

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,200
I'm not the right guy.

3
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:15,400
I had a great time with you.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,733
Goodbye, Takoi-san.

5
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:31,033
Shiono!

6
00:00:32,133 --> 00:00:34,233
What do you mean, goodbye?

7
00:00:35,367 --> 00:00:36,367
What?

8
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:39,167
Wait... Wait a minute!

9
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:44,567
Hey!

10
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:45,800
Shiono!

11
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,133
What the hell...

12
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,333
Huh?

13
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:54,133
What's wrong, Takoi?

14
00:00:54,433 --> 00:00:55,767
Do you have the guts?

15
00:00:55,867 --> 00:00:57,333
Huh?

16
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:02,000
Do you have the guts to kiss me right here?

17
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:02,933
What?

18
00:01:03,033 --> 00:01:04,300
Huh?

19
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,767
Takoi, are you serious?

20
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:07,300
Are you for real?

21
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,800
So you really are into guys!

22
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:10,900
Kiss him!

23
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,433
Huh?

24
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:21,700
Just as I thought, Takoi-san
and I aren't a good match.

25
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,433
That's all there is to it.

26
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:27,500
Goodbye.

27
00:01:28,367 --> 00:01:29,967
Wait a minute, Shiono!

28
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:34,200
Shiono...

29
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,733
Shiono!

30
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:45,567
What the hell...

31
00:02:14,967 --> 00:02:18,067
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

32
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:23,133
(Episode 6)

33
00:02:36,267 --> 00:02:37,633
Good morning.

34
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:40,167
Good morning.

35
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:05,967
Good morning.

36
00:03:07,567 --> 00:03:09,133
Good morning.

37
00:03:09,467 --> 00:03:10,967
You're too loud.

38
00:03:11,067 --> 00:03:12,667
Uh...

39
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:14,467
Are you tailing someone?

40
00:03:15,367 --> 00:03:16,676
Do I look like I'm tailing someone?

41
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,600
Because you look so serious.

42
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,267
Do I?

43
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:20,567
Yeah.

44
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:24,933
I'll go with you.

45
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:26,233
Huh?

46
00:03:28,533 --> 00:03:29,867
Hurry up.

47
00:03:38,733 --> 00:03:40,067
Good work.

48
00:03:40,833 --> 00:03:42,367
Congratulations on your promotion.

49
00:03:42,467 --> 00:03:43,667
Thank you.

50
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,133
A promotion is great news,
but I'll still miss you.

51
00:03:46,233 --> 00:03:47,133
Yeah.

52
00:03:47,233 --> 00:03:49,567
Best of luck at your new post.

53
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:55,433
You'll miss him?

54
00:03:55,533 --> 00:03:56,733
Huh?

55
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:57,967
No...

56
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,467
That's not it.

57
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:01,500
I'm just jealous of him.

58
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,067
Listen up, Takoi.

59
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:10,567
Getting promoted isn't everything in life.

60
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,867
- I really don't think that way.
- I know, I know you best.

61
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:15,367
Still, it must be nice.

62
00:04:15,467 --> 00:04:19,467
Shiono is definitely going
to keep climbing the ladder.

63
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,433
Then why don't you give
it a shot too, Takoi-san?

64
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:24,833
He knows it's not that easy.

65
00:04:24,933 --> 00:04:26,033
Exactly.

66
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:28,267
But it's not entirely impossible, right?

67
00:04:28,367 --> 00:04:31,600
Not impossible, just really hard.

68
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,400
But...

69
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,433
It's completely impossible for me.

70
00:04:36,933 --> 00:04:39,100
Are you really okay with
leaving things like this?

71
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,567
What?

72
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,740
You should have just gone after him.

73
00:04:50,133 --> 00:04:51,633
Hey, Shiono.

74
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,167
Here.

75
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,433
What's this?

76
00:04:58,533 --> 00:04:59,967
A farewell gift.

77
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:01,400
Though I already read it.

78
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:02,700
"How to Show a Natural Smile."

79
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:05,527
Is my smile really that unnatural?

80
00:05:05,567 --> 00:05:08,233
I just figured that once you go to HQ,

81
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:10,309
you might find it even harder
to smile than you do now.

82
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:11,433
True.

83
00:05:11,667 --> 00:05:14,367
A smile is the lubricant of the soul.

84
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,000
What kind of logic is that?

85
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,467
Thanks.

86
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:24,767
Yeah.

87
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,667
Is there something else?

88
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,567
No, nothing.

89
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:51,367
Hmm?

90
00:05:52,167 --> 00:05:53,467
It's nothing.

91
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,300
What's wrong?

92
00:06:01,533 --> 00:06:02,600
Takoi-san.

93
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:03,833
Hmm?

94
00:06:04,433 --> 00:06:06,033
Are you really okay with how things are?

95
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,600
What?

96
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:09,567
I know it's none of my business.

97
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:13,233
But are you really okay
with leaving things like this?

98
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:15,500
Shiono is getting transferred.

99
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,133
Once he's gone, it'll be
hard to see him again.

100
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:22,513
If there's still any bad blood between
you two, you'd better clear it up soon.

101
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:25,067
I know.

102
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:28,500
I know all that.

103
00:06:34,267 --> 00:06:35,400
Geez.

104
00:07:02,433 --> 00:07:03,733
What are you doing here?

105
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,167
Well...

106
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,133
Nothing.

107
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:15,233
You haven't eaten yet, right?

108
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,167
If you don't mind, want
to grab a bite together?

109
00:07:20,733 --> 00:07:22,200
No thanks.

110
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,100
I see.

111
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,033
I'm really sorry.

112
00:07:34,633 --> 00:07:37,800
I said some terrible things to you.

113
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,667
But I didn't mean any of it.

114
00:07:42,767 --> 00:07:45,167
It was just the only thing
I could say at the time.

115
00:07:45,667 --> 00:07:47,900
Uh... No.

116
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,167
I'm not trying to make excuses for myself.

117
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,767
- So, I really...
- Takoi-san.

118
00:07:58,033 --> 00:08:00,100
I'm not mad.

119
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,667
Oh? Really?

120
00:08:06,067 --> 00:08:07,400
Yeah.

121
00:08:10,133 --> 00:08:11,267
No...

122
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,133
I know I was in the wrong.

123
00:08:14,233 --> 00:08:17,033
But you suddenly acted like
you wanted to cut ties with me.

124
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:18,567
So I panicked a little.

125
00:08:18,667 --> 00:08:19,967
That's why.

126
00:08:20,733 --> 00:08:23,867
I said, "Since we're not a
good match, let's just forget it."

127
00:08:23,967 --> 00:08:25,500
The two of us...

128
00:08:26,367 --> 00:08:29,300
That's all there is to it.

129
00:08:31,567 --> 00:08:34,900
Find someone you'd be
proud to introduce to anyone.

130
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Have a proper relationship,
and then get married.

131
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:43,867
I think that suits you better.

132
00:08:44,933 --> 00:08:46,467
Chief Takoi.

133
00:08:50,367 --> 00:08:51,533
That's all.

134
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,633
Shiono!

135
00:09:51,767 --> 00:09:52,567
Huh?

136
00:09:52,667 --> 00:09:54,100
Shiono-san?

137
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,700
Hello.

138
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:58,167
Huh?

139
00:09:58,267 --> 00:09:59,276
Since you're already passing by.

140
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:01,033
Come on, come in and sit for a bit.

141
00:10:01,133 --> 00:10:01,867
Wait...

142
00:10:01,967 --> 00:10:02,967
Let's go.

143
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:05,300
(Forte)

144
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:08,100
I heard you're getting transferred?

145
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,433
Yes.

146
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:11,767
To HQ, right?

147
00:10:11,867 --> 00:10:13,667
That's impressive.

148
00:10:13,767 --> 00:10:15,033
It's nothing.

149
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,767
But it'll be lonely once you're gone.

150
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:23,300
Takoi must be really sad to see you go too.

151
00:10:24,633 --> 00:10:26,067
Who knows.

152
00:10:28,633 --> 00:10:33,100
You two protected me in this
very shop before, didn't you?

153
00:10:33,533 --> 00:10:35,167
Brings back memories.

154
00:10:38,133 --> 00:10:39,600
That did happen.

155
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:40,700
Yeah.

156
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:43,267
Shiono-san, you were
really amazing back then.

157
00:10:43,367 --> 00:10:46,267
You just charged right
into the middle of it.

158
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:51,533
But because of that, you
ended up getting hurt.

159
00:10:52,333 --> 00:10:54,367
It's all Takoi-san's fault.

160
00:10:54,467 --> 00:10:55,867
He was way too defenseless.

161
00:10:59,167 --> 00:11:03,167
Seriously... he just makes
you worry about him.

162
00:11:05,933 --> 00:11:07,067
Yeah.

163
00:11:07,833 --> 00:11:10,233
He just can't leave other
people's business alone.

164
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:11,867
That's just how Takoi-san is.

165
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,300
I guess you could say he's
just not good at saying no.

166
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:18,700
Is that what you call a model detective?

167
00:11:21,733 --> 00:11:24,833
He's probably always been like that.

168
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,233
So gentle with everyone.

169
00:11:35,667 --> 00:11:38,147
And he's always so nice to
people, giving them the wrong idea.

170
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:44,800
But that's very much like him.

171
00:11:48,133 --> 00:11:50,767
He always gives it his all,
even when facing criminals.

172
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:56,167
He loves to act cool,

173
00:11:56,267 --> 00:11:58,600
but he actually has a cute side too.

174
00:12:01,033 --> 00:12:04,400
He freezes up completely
when he gets nervous.

175
00:12:05,953 --> 00:12:07,653
I'd expect nothing less from you.

176
00:12:07,967 --> 00:12:09,700
You really know him well.

177
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:12,200
But...

178
00:12:14,967 --> 00:12:17,467
We're just too different.

179
00:12:34,767 --> 00:12:36,200
I'm back.

180
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:51,667
Sorry I'm so late.

181
00:12:58,433 --> 00:13:01,133
(Reserved for Today)

182
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,833
Boss, another beer!

183
00:13:05,933 --> 00:13:07,033
Coming right up.

184
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,133
Exactly.
Not bad.

185
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:10,467
Eat up.

186
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:11,733
And another thing.

187
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,100
The difference is night and day.

188
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:17,700
Even when you go to HQ, don't forget about us
folks in the Criminal Investigation Division.

189
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:19,067
I'll try my best.

190
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:21,167
Man, you're so stiff.

191
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:23,600
But I like that about you.

192
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:28,100
Boss, one oolong tea and three more beers!

193
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:28,900
Got it.

194
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
- Eat up.
- Hurry and eat.

195
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,700
- Here.
- Yeah.

196
00:13:32,133 --> 00:13:34,767
Shiono is finally leaving, huh.

197
00:13:35,733 --> 00:13:36,733
Yeah...

198
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:38,000
Look at him.

199
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,567
Still so calm at a time like this.

200
00:13:39,667 --> 00:13:40,867
Not even drinking.

201
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,133
He's a total lightweight.

202
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:47,467
Yeah.

203
00:13:48,067 --> 00:13:49,800
You really know him well, huh?

204
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:50,967
What?

205
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:53,133
I've always thought this, Takoi.

206
00:13:54,533 --> 00:13:56,367
You and Shiono are pretty close, right?

207
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,867
I wouldn't say we're close...

208
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,433
Hmm?

209
00:14:04,567 --> 00:14:05,567
What?

210
00:14:05,667 --> 00:14:08,767
Of course they're close.

211
00:14:08,867 --> 00:14:10,533
Takoi-san and Shiono.

212
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,533
Right?

213
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,700
No way.

214
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,400
I can't drink anymore.

215
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,733
Alright, it's about time...

216
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,200
The party's winding down.

217
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,533
Takoi!

218
00:14:42,033 --> 00:14:43,033
Yes?

219
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,833
This is your time to shine.

220
00:14:44,933 --> 00:14:46,300
Our ultimate hype man.

221
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,400
What?!

222
00:14:47,467 --> 00:14:49,467
Say a few words of
encouragement for Shiono.

223
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:50,567
Come on.

224
00:14:50,667 --> 00:14:52,300
Takoi! Go for it!

225
00:15:09,267 --> 00:15:12,100
Shiono might be a bit aloof,

226
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,433
but he's an outstanding cop.

227
00:15:15,533 --> 00:15:17,200
I'm sure you've all heard that by now.

228
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:20,300
Even the folks in other departments.

229
00:15:22,233 --> 00:15:24,000
Hey, that's too stiff!

230
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,467
Way too stiff!

231
00:15:25,967 --> 00:15:30,500
He's the elite assigned to the Community Safety
Division at Yama-no-michi Station.

232
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:33,833
Ridiculously handsome,
and most importantly, young!

233
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:38,133
Agh, he has everything I don't.

234
00:15:38,233 --> 00:15:40,733
What a guy to be jealous of.

235
00:15:40,833 --> 00:15:43,133
You're terrible.

236
00:15:44,833 --> 00:15:49,000
Alright... jokes aside, seriously.

237
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:52,967
Shiono isn't just a great detective.

238
00:15:53,067 --> 00:15:55,000
He's also an incredible guy.

239
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:58,100
I deal with him a lot,
both professionally and personally.

240
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,000
Even to me, he really is...

241
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:08,000
He really... really...

242
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,633
He might look cold,

243
00:16:16,533 --> 00:16:18,433
but he's actually very sentimental.

244
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,067
And gentle.

245
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:28,800
And straightforward.

246
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:37,600
I've been helped by
Shiono many times myself.

247
00:16:39,667 --> 00:16:40,967
Having him around

248
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:45,800
really puts you at ease.

249
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:06,433
Yeah...

250
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:23,100
I have something to say.

251
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:28,167
Wait... hold on...

252
00:17:28,267 --> 00:17:29,367
Where are you going?

253
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:32,600
What a touching bromance.

254
00:17:33,933 --> 00:17:36,633
So that's how it is.

255
00:17:37,067 --> 00:17:38,400
Yep.

256
00:17:39,467 --> 00:17:40,167
Alright!

257
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:44,267
Okay, next up is the karaoke contest!

258
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:47,267
Boss, turn on the karaoke, please.

259
00:17:47,367 --> 00:17:48,833
We don't have karaoke here.

260
00:17:49,433 --> 00:17:51,500
- Is that so?
- Then let's sing a cappella.

261
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:53,467
- Sounds good.
- Okay.

262
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:54,633
Then Yagi-san is up.

263
00:17:57,067 --> 00:17:58,833
Where exactly are you taking me?

264
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:03,833
People are going to get suspicious...

265
00:18:03,933 --> 00:18:05,700
I don't care about that!

266
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,000
I like you.

267
00:18:09,867 --> 00:18:11,233
It's you.

268
00:18:16,133 --> 00:18:18,033
I'm the one who's truly disgusting.

269
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:27,333
In the end, you're all I can think about.

270
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,233
But...

271
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:32,667
I didn't want anyone to see through me.

272
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:37,367
And I didn't want anyone to
know I was head over heels.

273
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,467
Going on dates with you is fun.

274
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:44,400
Being with you makes my heart race.

275
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:47,833
I just felt...

276
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:53,700
it was embarrassing for
people around us to know.

277
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,933
But...

278
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,367
But I...

279
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:06,467
didn't consider your feelings at all.

280
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,467
I don't want it to end like this.

281
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,200
I really can't take it anymore.

282
00:19:31,033 --> 00:19:33,533
I have no idea what to do.

283
00:19:33,633 --> 00:19:35,533
I'm completely lost.

284
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,533
Why...

285
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,300
Do you know what you're saying?

286
00:20:02,567 --> 00:20:05,167
I even went out of my
way to leave you an out.

287
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,100
Hey.

288
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:19,533
You're finally awake.

289
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,433
Good morning, Kamekichi.

290
00:21:32,667 --> 00:21:33,900
Takoi-san.

291
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,333
Hmm?

292
00:21:35,733 --> 00:21:38,667
You have sleep marks on your face.

293
00:21:38,767 --> 00:21:40,267
Huh? Really?

294
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:41,733
Where?

295
00:21:41,833 --> 00:21:43,133
Hmm?

296
00:21:50,033 --> 00:21:51,333
Right here.

297
00:21:54,767 --> 00:21:56,200
You drank too much.

298
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,600
At your age, you should pace yourself.

299
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:00,067
You little...

300
00:22:06,433 --> 00:22:07,533
Good morning.

301
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,033
Good morning.

302
00:22:14,067 --> 00:22:16,000
I heard a turtle's ears are right here.

303
00:22:17,133 --> 00:22:17,900
Where?

304
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,267
- Here.
- Huh? Which one?

305
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:21,600
Around the back here...

306
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:22,933
Huh? This?

307
00:22:23,033 --> 00:22:24,833
That's not an ear.

308
00:22:24,933 --> 00:22:26,009
It's just a pattern, right?

309
00:22:26,033 --> 00:22:27,167
It's an ear.

310
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:31,243
(Next Episode) This is Omaeda, who's replacing
Shiono in the Community Safety Division.

311
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:32,543
I heard he's from Internal Affairs.

312
00:22:32,567 --> 00:22:34,143
There's a police station in the prefecture.

313
00:22:34,167 --> 00:22:35,767
I heard internal data was leaked.

314
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:37,843
I'm Date, in charge of
directing Internal Affairs.

315
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:38,767
Nice to meet you.
Ouch!

316
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,933
I heard you've been
taking good care of our Shu.

317
00:22:42,033 --> 00:22:43,067
Ah...

318
00:22:43,167 --> 00:22:46,367
Stop calling me Shiono.
Call me by my first name.

319
00:22:46,467 --> 00:22:47,733
Shu...

320
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:48,833
Not bad, right?
